Source: pg-stat-tcpinfo
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/jakubwartakEDB/pg_stat_tcpinfo

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-stat-tcpinfo
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-stat-tcpinfo
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Detailed Linux TCP socket statistics for PostgreSQL
 Expose TCP connections owned by the PostgreSQL server OS user, including
 round-trip time, retransmissions, congestion control and queue statistics.
 Requires Linux 4.18 or newer with procfs and NETLINK_INET_DIAG.
 Access is restricted to PostgreSQL monitoring roles; no preload is needed.
